{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791429211,"nonce":"WsT66ngTjMOZVsdOWsvh0DGbXIo=","title":"Cranelift: preserve HIR cold-call hints in native block layout","message":"HIR FunctionAttributes.cold is populated by frontend annotations and used by the inliner and promotion policy, but Cranelift does not propagate it to the blocks that call those functions. Rare error helpers therefore have ordinary block frequency and layout. In the NUC LU native dump, repeated bounds-check branches lead to large error-return paths; these currently receive no cold marking.\n\nForward direct calls to a known cold HIR function into FunctionBuilder::set_cold_block. This is a layout/frequency hint only: cold calls must remain executable and preserve their return values. Validate generated CLIF and both branch results, then compare whole-process times with a same-executable disable control and preserve interpreter-first OSR. Do not infer coldness from benchmark names or from arbitrary calls.","files":null}]}